<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federal Charter of 1291</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1291</span> · Also known as Bundesbrief</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Federal Charter of 1291 is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> alliance document dated to early August 1291, in which the valley communities of Uri, Schwyz and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nidwalden">Nidwalden</a> promised each other aid against outside attack and agreed rules for keeping the peace and settling disputes. Rediscovered in the 18th century, it came to be treated as the founding document of the Swiss Confederation. It is kept in Schwyz, and 1 August is the Swiss National Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federal-charter-of-1291.jpg" alt="Federal Charter of 1291" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesbrief.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
